+--------------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
| Safety Precaution / Tool       | Why It Is Important                          |
+--------------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
| Turn off the PC                | Prevents electrical shock and damage.        |
| Unplug the power cable         | Removes power before opening the cabinet.    |
| Use an anti-static wrist strap | Protects components from static electricity. |
| Keep screws in a container     | Stops screws from getting lost.              |
| Use proper lighting            | Helps identify ports, cables, and screws.    |
| Handle parts by the edges      | Prevents touching sensitive circuits.        |
| Do not force connectors        | Prevents damage to ports and connectors.     |
| Take photos before removal     | Helps remember cable and component positions.|
| Keep cables organized          | Makes reassembly easier and safer.           |
| Check connections before power | Prevents loose cables from causing problems. |
+--------------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
